amJMNUM5azhr?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -4.79, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": -1.39, "poll_sd": 9.89, "poll_weight": 0.21, "fundamentals": {"margin": 0.01, "lean": -7.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.19}, "rating_margin": -8.0, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.22, "baseline_margin": -4.08, "analyst_adjustment": 1.08, "key_factors": ["District's R+7 partisan lean in an open seat", "Flippo's Bronze Star misrepresentation scandal reported by the Washington Post", "Near-even polling but thin, dated, and partly Democratic-sponsored", "Benitez-Thompson's national Democratic backing versus Flippo's large cash and outside-spending edge"], "rationale": "The district's R+7 lean and a Likely R consensus from most raters anchor the forecast toward Republicans, but the open seat, Flippo's Bronze Star controversy, and polls showing a near-tied race justify shading the margin a few points closer than the fundamentals alone imply. Markets still price the Republican around 80%, consistent with a modest GOP edge.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling or a sustained wave environment for Democrats could tighten this further, while the scandal's staying power will test whether Flippo's financial advantage holds.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mark Amodei (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Mark Amodei's retirement leaves this R+7 northern Nevada seat open, giving Democrats their best shot at it in years. State Senator Teresa Benitez-Thompson has drawn national party backing, while Republican David Flippo has far out-raised her and enjoys a large outside-spending advantage. Most expert raters call the race Likely R, though two rate it Lean R and one calls it a Tossup.\n\nPolling is sparse and mostly from early September, but it shows a surprisingly close contest, with one Democratic-sponsored poll putting the candidates even. Flippo faces damaging coverage over exaggerating his Bronze Star record, and Benitez-Thompson faces attacks of her own over past votes. The fundamentals still favor Republicans, but the open seat and the scandal keep this competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.213, "margin": -4.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2977, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2868, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2952, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2127, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2908, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3379, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3508, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3896, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3448, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3118, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2576, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2807, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1915, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2968, "margin": -3.0}]}